From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Onyx contributors <onyx@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:33:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/24] Onyx: PAL and WebCore build (step 2 of the port): Skia
 on the CPU, no GL, curl, the Adwaita theme

What:
- cmake/OptionsOnyx.cmake: ONYX_WEBCORE (off: the jsc shell alone) turns ENABLE_WEBCORE on, with
  the sysroot's static libraries imported by hand in link order (zlib, brotli, mbedTLS, nghttp2,
  curl, libpng, libjpeg, libwebp, FreeType, HarfBuzz, libxml2, SQLite, Skia with its include
  layout and the definitions of its skia.pc), USE_SKIA / USE_CURL / USE_HARFBUZZ / USE_MBEDTLS /
  USE_THEME_ADWAITA on, USE_SKIA_GPU off, no TextureMapper / Coordinated Graphics / EGL / libwpe,
  video, Web Audio, WebGL, the GPU process, async scrolling, XSLT, WOFF2 (libwoff2) off.
- Source/CMakeLists.txt: ThirdParty/skia is not added when the port brings a Skia::Skia target.
  WebCore/CMakeLists.txt: no GLES / EGL link for Onyx.
- WebCore/PlatformOnyx.cmake, PAL/pal/PlatformOnyx.cmake: Adwaita, curl, the image decoders,
  Skia; the generic and Unix files; Onyx's own:
  accessibility/onyx (no system accessibility yet: no-ops), platform/graphics/onyx
  (GraphicsLayerOnyx: GraphicsLayer::create with a layer that draws nothing -- no compositor,
  accelerated compositing stays off --, SystemFontDatabaseOnyx), platform/network/onyx
  (CurlSSLHandleOnyx: the CA bundle SD:/res/ca-bundle; NetworkStateNotifierOnyx;
  PublicSuffixStoreOnyx: an interim rule, no public suffix list yet), platform/onyx
  (MIMETypeRegistryOnyx, PlatformScreenOnyx, UserAgentOnyx, PlatformKeyboardEventOnyx).
- PLATFORM(ONYX) beside the ports it behaves like: AXCoreObject.h (the empty wrapper),
  Pasteboard.h / PasteboardStrategy.h / StaticPasteboard.cpp and the libwpe pasteboard and editor
  files (they call no libwpe function: shared), FontCache / FontCacheSkia /
  SkiaSystemFallbackFontCache (Onyx's SkFontMgr_New_Onyx instead of fontconfig, the Android /
  Windows side of the guards).
- page/Page.cpp: Settings::hardwareAccelerationEnabled only where it is declared (GTK, WPE
  platform).

Why: WebCore for a system with no GL, no GLib, no fontconfig, no OpenSSL: pages are laid out
and painted by Skia on the CPU into a bitmap. With this libWebCore.a builds and a test program
links and renders a page (HTML, CSS, SVG, canvas, scripts) under qemu.
